{
  "id": "dianju_yunnan_opera",
  "name": "Dianju (Yunnan opera)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Opera of Yunnan centred on Kunming, sung in Yunnan dialect, whose three main tune systems are sixian (from Qinqiang bangzi), huqin (from the shipai tune of Hui opera, akin to erhuang) and xiangyang (from the Xianghe school of Han opera, akin to xipi); it entered China's national intangible heritage list in 2008. Sixian tunes are led by the juqin, a wood-faced fiddle close to the Qinqiang erguxian (the banhu card stands in), and huqin and xiangyang tunes by a huqin (the erhu card stands in), with drum, gong and cymbals.",
  "recipe": "classic late-2000s dianju, art Music, east Asian branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment, single lead single track no stacking. gutty bowl resonator coconut shell paulownia banhu, erhu, membrane drum pulse resonant acoustic membrane drum, opera bending gong tamtam, naobo. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
